From c7b26a089cdb717d73818409a9877e63f53a0bba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergio Marin <sergio.marin@pantacor.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 18:55:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rdawlan: import the vendor RDA599x cfg80211 driver

Verbatim import of the vendor 3.10 rdawlan driver from
OrangePiLibra/OrangePi_i96_kernel@74c4ea44, reduced to the SDIO station
path: no USB, no BT-AMP, no P2P (already off in the vendor's own
wland_defs.h), no wireless-extensions, no Android private commands, no
monitor mode. Those carry the worst API rot and none are needed for a
working wlan0.

The chip 'firmware' is a table of register patches compiled in from
wland_trap_91g.h, not a blob, and the whole driver is under a permissive
ISC-style licence -- so there is nothing to fetch at runtime and nothing
with unclear redistribution terms.

This commit is the unmodified import so that the forward-port to 6.6 is
reviewable as a separate diff on top.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [local forward-port of vendor driver]
